# Normalise line endings in the repo; check out native on each machine.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. This repo is edited from Windows (in a OneDrive folder)
# and written to by a Linux GitHub Actions runner every morning. Without
# this file the two disagree about line endings, and every file either
# side touches comes back as a whole-file diff.
#
# Measured on 27 Aug 2026, before this file existed:
#
#   src/app/bridal-jewellery/page.tsx   522 insertions, 522 deletions
#   src/app/elite-plan/page.tsx         554 insertions, 554 deletions
#   data/rates-state.json               117 changed lines
#   public/rates.json                    16 changed lines
#
#   Real content changes in all four: ZERO. Verified by parsing both
#   versions of the JSON and comparing, and by `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol`
#   coming back empty.
#
# That is not a cosmetic annoyance. It means a genuine one-line edit and a
# line-ending change look identical in `git status`, so a real change can
# be reviewed as noise and discarded — or noise committed as though it
# were a change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff.
*.webp binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.avif binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
